Every first-3-month-opioid-use-disorder-risk-increase-point-evidence is insufficient.
If a clinician reassesses a pain-and-function within 1 month of an opioid-initiation then the clinician gains a treatment-plan-modification-opportunity for a pain-treatment-goal-achievement.
If a clinician reassesses a pain-and-function within 1 month of an opioid-initiation and a patient does not receive a clear-opioid-benefit then the clinician gains a taper-and-discontinuation-long-term-opioid-use-risk-minimization-opportunity for the patient.
A pain-treatment-goal-example is a functional-goal-example.
